then need W7-W8-W9 or W6-W7-W8 \u2014 but W7 is nearly gone.\n- W8 is dangerous because opponent already has [W6, W7, W8] melded \u2014 they may be waiting on W8 or W9.\n- T3 could complete another bamboo chow, but I only have T2 and T3, and T1 is already used \u2014 not helpful.\n- B7 is isolated \u2014 no obvious chow unless I had B5-B6 or B6-B8, but B4 is gone and B6 is low.\n\nSafer discards: Among valid actions, **Play W1** stands out. W1 is a terminal tile, hard to use in a chow unless someone needs 1-2-3, but I have no W2 or W3. It doesn\u2019t contribute to any potential straight. Also, W1 has 3 remaining \u2014 not completely dead, but keeping it blocks progress.\n\nAlternatively, **Play B7**: B7 could be part of 5-6-7 or 6-7-8 or 7-8-9, but I have no supporting tiles. But B7 has 3 remaining, so not fully safe.\n\nBut note: I already have **J1 pung (2 pts)**. If I can get **Self Drawn (1 pt)** and say **Single Wait / Closed Wait (2 pts)**, plus **All Chows (2 pts)**, that\u2019s 7 \u2014 still short. Need more.\n\nWait types:\n- If I end up with a closed wait on W5 (to complete W4-W5-W6), that gives **Closed Wait (2 pts)**.\n- If I draw the winning tile myself, **Self Drawn (1 pt)**.\n- **All Chows (2 pts)**: Yes, if final hand has four chows and a pair.\n- So if I can convert my J1 pung into something else? No \u2014 already exposed via Peng.\n\nAh \u2014 **Peng J1** means it's an exposed pung. So I cannot count **Fully Concealed Hand**, but **All Chows** requires *only* chows and a pair \u2014 I have a pung, so **All Chows is impossible**.\n\nTherefore, **All Chows is invalid** due to having a pung (J1).\n\nSo strategy shifts: I must accept the pung. Best shot is to go for **Half Flush** (honor + one suit) or try **Mixed Triple Chow** or **Pure Straight**.\n\nBut suits are mixed: I have J1 (honor), T1-T2-T3 (Bamboo), and W tiles (Characters). So too many suits.\n\nBetter idea: minimize risk and aim for **Chicken Hand (8 pts)** \u2014 which is a baseline 8